<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil, meal firm.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil, meal firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were almost steady on a firm note, dealers said on Wednesday. Trade was dull due to limited availability. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on limited supply against good demand in local market. Soyoil prices rose 400 rupees per tonne. Business volume was good and the undertone firm.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained firm on limited supply. Soymeal yellow was $320 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export which was around $220 per tonne at the same time last year.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $124 per tonne FAS in export and was 4,250 rupees per tonne FOR (Free On Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
